WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.622
Dominoes. Quick Starter.
 
00:00:02.682 --> 00:00:06.252
Sherlock Holmes. The Dying Detective.
 
00:00:06.312 --> 00:00:08.662
By Sir Arthur Conan Doyle.

00:00:08.722 --> 00:00:24.200
Adapted by Lesley Thompson. Read by Danica Fairman, Rob Fitch. Wayne Forrester. Roger May and James Daniel Wilson. Published and copyright Oxford University Press 2016.
 
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Chapter One. Holmes is ill.
 
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.000
It is 1890 in London.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:51.100
At 221b Baker Street, Mrs Hudson, Sherlock Holmes's servant, is sad.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.671
Things are very bad.

00:00:53.731 --> 00:00:57.288
Holmes is dying!

00:00:57.348 --> 00:01:04.830
Three days now, and he is worse! she thinks.

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:13.086
Mrs Hudson likes Holmes very much but she is also a little afraid of him.

00:01:13.146 --> 00:01:15.538
He is different.

00:01:15.598 --> 00:01:23.943
He has strange visitors and they come at all hours of the day and night.

00:01:24.002 --> 00:01:29.196
His rooms have many strange things in them.

00:01:29.256 --> 00:01:33.130
But he is very nice to Mrs Hudson.

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:39.266
She respects him and she does not want to lose him.

00:01:39.326 --> 00:01:44.961
I must visit Dr Watson, she thinks.

00:01:45.021 --> 00:01:47.906
He can help.

00:01:47.965 --> 00:01:55.722
At this time, Dr Watson is living in a different street in London.

00:01:55.782 --> 00:02:00.795
Mrs Hudson goes quickly to his rooms.

00:02:00.855 --> 00:02:08.640
Dr Watson! she cries when the doctor opens the door to her.
 
00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:13.362
Please come with me. It's Mr Holmes.
 
00:02:13.422 --> 00:02:19.828
He's dying! What? Watson cries.
 
00:02:19.888 --> 00:02:23.409
I know nothing about this!

00:02:23.469 --> 00:02:30.081
He doesn't want a doctor but you must come, sir.

00:02:30.141 --> 00:02:36.083
After three days, he's very, very ill.

00:02:36.143 --> 00:02:40.234
He's saying strange things.

00:02:40.294 --> 00:02:43.005
I'm afraid for him.

00:02:43.065 --> 00:02:45.748
You must be quick!

00:02:45.808 --> 00:02:52.486
Watson gets his coat and bag and they leave the house.

00:02:52.545 --> 00:02:59.144
In the cab, he asks Mrs Hudson some more questions.

00:02:59.204 --> 00:03:02.510
I can't tell you much, sir.

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:09.066
Lately, Mr Holmes is working in Rotherhithe, near the river.

00:03:09.126 --> 00:03:14.490
He comes home and he brings this illness with him.

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:17.544
He's much worse now.

00:03:17.604 --> 00:03:30.800
Can he live through this?

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:44.100
Chapter Two. Watson cannot help.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:52.760
When they arrive at Baker Street on that dark November day, Holmes is alive. 

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:57.704
But Watson is afraid for his friend.

00:03:57.764 --> 00:04:06.264
The detective's face is yellow, and his eyes are red with fever.

00:04:06.324 --> 00:04:10.446
His hands move without stopping.

00:04:10.506 --> 00:04:15.017
When he speaks, his voice is weak.

00:04:15.077 --> 00:04:21.140
Well, Watson, bad days are here, I think.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.980
He smiles weakly.

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:27.072
My poor man!

00:04:27.131 --> 00:04:32.355
cries Watson and he moves towards the bed.

00:04:32.414 --> 00:04:35.439
Don't come near me!

00:04:35.498 --> 00:04:40.864
But why? I only want to help.
 
00:04:40.924 --> 00:04:44.968
I know, but you can't help me.

00:04:45.028 --> 00:04:53.004
My illness is from the Far East and it's very contagious.

00:04:53.064 --> 00:04:58.908
I'm a doctor, says Watson quietly.

00:04:58.968 --> 00:05:02.970
These things don't matter to me.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:08.014
Don't move, and I can talk to you.

00:05:08.074 --> 00:05:13.800
If not, you must leave the room now.

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:20.266
Holmes looks at Watson with fever in his eyes.

00:05:20.326 --> 00:05:24.679
I can't trust you with this, Watson.

00:05:24.739 --> 00:05:30.122
You know nothing of these strange illnesses.

00:05:30.182 --> 00:05:36.436
Do you know about Tapanuli fever, for example?

00:05:36.496 --> 00:05:40.270
Or the Black Formosa fever?

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:42.921
No, you don't.

00:05:42.981 --> 00:05:46.414
You aren't a specialist.

00:05:46.474 --> 00:05:54.060
I'm sorry to say this, but I must see a specialist.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:06:03.328
Watson is not happy at these words, but he also respects the detective.

00:06:03.388 --> 00:06:06.810
Very well, Holmes.

00:06:06.869 --> 00:06:16.045
Dr Ainstree, the best specialist in these illnesses, is now in London.

00:06:16.105 --> 00:06:19.627
I'm going to him now.

00:06:19.687 --> 00:06:24.061
Watson walks towards the door.

00:06:24.121 --> 00:06:28.774
Suddenly, Holmes is out of bed.

00:06:28.834 --> 00:06:34.535
He goes quickly to the door and locks it.

00:06:34.595 --> 00:06:40.586
Then he goes very slowly back to bed.

00:06:40.646 --> 00:06:45.797
Watson looks at his friend in shock.

00:06:45.856 --> 00:06:59.800
What is the matter with Holmes?

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:14.500
Chapter Three. Holmes is worse.

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:17.272
Holmes cries excitedly:

00:07:17.292 --> 00:07:20.855
Stay here, Watson!

00:07:20.914 --> 00:07:23.406
I've got the key!

00:07:23.466 --> 00:07:25.857
What time is it?

00:07:25.917 --> 00:07:27.946
Four o'clock?

00:07:28.006 --> 00:07:34.586
At six o'clock you can go, but not before!

00:07:34.646 --> 00:07:39.248
Watson looks at his friend sadly.

00:07:39.308 --> 00:07:47.142
Holmes, this illness is doing strange things to your head.

00:07:47.201 --> 00:07:51.924
But I can wait until six.

00:07:51.984 --> 00:07:56.526
Good! One more thing, Watson.
 
00:07:56.586 --> 00:08:01.200
Don't bring that man, Ainstree.

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:07.372
Now, perhaps I can sleep a little.

00:08:07.432 --> 00:08:15.356
Watson waits, looking at the pictures and books in the room.

00:08:15.416 --> 00:08:21.500
On a table, he sees a little black and white box.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:27.572
That's interesting, he thinks.
 
00:08:27.631 --> 00:08:31.523
He moves his hand towards it.

00:08:31.582 --> 00:08:37.046
Suddenly, a terrible cry comes from the bed.

00:08:37.106 --> 00:08:39.589
Stop, Watson!

00:08:39.648 --> 00:08:42.662
Don't move my things.

00:08:42.722 --> 00:08:45.204
I don't like it.

00:08:45.264 --> 00:08:47.900
Sit down, man!

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:57.600
I need to sleep!

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:06.051
At six o'clock, Holmes says, Let's have some light, Watson.

00:09:06.111 --> 00:09:09.022
But only a little!

00:09:09.082 --> 00:09:12.574
Put the box near me.

00:09:12.634 --> 00:09:15.385
Not with your hands!

00:09:15.445 --> 00:09:18.186
Use your handkerchief!

00:09:18.246 --> 00:09:20.361
That's right.

00:09:20.421 --> 00:09:29.828
Now you can go to Mr Culverton Smith of 13 Lower Burke Street.

00:09:29.888 --> 00:09:33.938
But who is this man, Holmes?

00:09:33.998 --> 00:09:36.829
I don't know the name.

00:09:36.889 --> 00:09:39.580
He isn't a doctor.

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:47.402
He has a plantation in Sumatra but he's visiting London.

00:09:47.462 --> 00:09:55.494
He knows this illness well because his workers often have it.

00:09:55.554 --> 00:10:00.596
Things are not good between us.

00:10:00.656 --> 00:10:07.060
Smith's nephew, Victor Savage, is dead.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:13.752
There is something wrong about his terrible death.

00:10:13.812 --> 00:10:17.052
I don't trust Smith.

00:10:17.112 --> 00:10:19.462
And he knows it.

00:10:19.522 --> 00:10:24.172
But only he can help me.

00:10:24.233 --> 00:10:28.093
There is one more thing.

00:10:28.153 --> 00:10:31.614
Don't come back with him.

00:10:31.674 --> 00:10:35.435
You must be here before him.

00:10:35.495 --> 00:10:39.916
This is very important, Watson.

00:10:39.976 --> 00:10:46.082
Watson takes the key, and he goes into the street.

00:10:46.142 --> 00:10:51.498
He sees Inspector Morton of Scotland Yard.

00:10:51.558 --> 00:10:57.051
How is Mr Holmes, sir? Morton asks.
 
00:10:57.111 --> 00:11:03.034
He's very ill. Watson answers.
 
00:11:03.094 --> 00:11:07.236
Morton smiles strangely.

00:11:07.296 --> 00:11:12.522
I know something about it. He says.
 
00:11:12.582 --> 00:11:18.338
Watson doesn't understand, but he cannot wait.

00:11:18.398 --> 00:11:35.200
He gets into a cab and leaves.

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:47.300
Chapter Four. The specialist. 

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:54.434
At 13 Lower Burke Street, A servant answers the door.
  
00:11:54.494 --> 00:11:58.137
Watson goes into the house.

00:11:58.196 --> 00:12:02.220
He can hear Culverton Smith's voice.

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:04.842
Oh, it is Watson!

00:12:04.902 --> 00:12:06.942
What does he want?

00:12:07.002 --> 00:12:09.184
I need to work.

00:12:09.244 --> 00:12:12.014
I cannot see him.

00:12:12.074 --> 00:12:15.774
Watson thinks of Holmes.

00:12:15.834 --> 00:12:20.076
Quickly, he goes into the room.

00:12:20.136 --> 00:12:25.868
The man in the room stands up from his chair.

00:12:25.928 --> 00:12:30.811
Watson sees his dark, angry eyes.

00:12:30.871 --> 00:12:35.162
What's this? The man cries.
 
00:12:35.222 --> 00:12:38.324
I'm sorry, says Watson.

00:12:38.384 --> 00:12:41.113
But I can't wait.

00:12:41.174 --> 00:12:45.394
It's about Mr Sherlock Holmes.

00:12:45.454 --> 00:12:50.046
Culverton Smith's face changes.

00:12:50.106 --> 00:12:53.857
He watches Watson carefully.

00:12:53.917 --> 00:12:57.098
What about Holmes?

00:12:57.158 --> 00:12:59.189
How is he?

00:12:59.249 --> 00:13:03.410
He's very ill.

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:06.842
Watson sits down.

00:13:06.902 --> 00:13:11.653
Is that a smile on Smith's face?

00:13:11.713 --> 00:13:17.100
I'm sorry to hear this, Smith says.
 
00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:23.830
I don't know Holmes well, but I respect him.

00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:26.932
We're not very different.

00:13:26.992 --> 00:13:33.646
He studies criminals and I study microbes.

00:13:33.706 --> 00:13:43.000
He looks at the bottles on the table next to him and laughs.

00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:48.799
Holmes needs you, Watson says.
 
00:13:48.859 --> 00:13:54.970
Why? Is his illness from the Far East?

00:13:55.030 --> 00:14:03.100
Perhaps. His work lately is with people from there.

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:08.222
Oh, I see. Smith smiles.
 
00:14:08.282 --> 00:14:11.500
How many days is it now?

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:14.802
About three?

00:14:14.862 --> 00:14:17.614
Is he thinking well?

00:14:17.674 --> 00:14:20.286
Not always.

00:14:20.346 --> 00:14:22.488
That is bad.

00:14:22.548 --> 00:14:25.971
I must go and help him.

00:14:26.031 --> 00:14:30.554
Watson remembers Holmes' words.

00:14:30.614 --> 00:14:35.500
He says, I can't go with you.

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:38.366
I need to make a visit.

00:14:38.426 --> 00:14:41.711
Very well, Smith says.

00:14:41.771 --> 00:14:56.600
I can be there in half an hour.

00:14:56.700 --> 00:15:11.400
Chapter Five. A killer at Baker Street. 

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:18.422
Watson runs into Holmes's room. Is he coming?
 
00:15:18.542 --> 00:15:22.836
Holmes asks. Yes, he is.

00:15:22.896 --> 00:15:25.598
Very good, Watson!

00:15:25.658 --> 00:15:30.402
Now you must hide behind the bed.

00:15:30.462 --> 00:15:33.834
Don't speak or move.

00:15:33.894 --> 00:15:39.262
Just listen very carefully.

00:15:39.322 --> 00:15:46.291
Watson hides behind the bed and waits.

00:15:46.352 --> 00:15:51.694
Soon he hears Culverton Smith's voice.

00:15:51.754 --> 00:15:55.646
Can you hear me, Holmes?

00:15:55.706 --> 00:16:00.168
Is that you, Mr Smith?

00:16:00.228 --> 00:16:03.510
Holmes says weakly.

00:16:03.570 --> 00:16:06.732
Thank you for coming.

00:16:06.792 --> 00:16:11.100
Smith laughs.

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:14.874
What's the matter with you, Holmes?

00:16:14.934 --> 00:16:19.246
It's Victor's illness, I think.

00:16:19.306 --> 00:16:22.708
Yes! My nephew!
 
00:16:22.768 --> 00:16:31.704
Four days ill and he's dead! Smith laughs again.
 
00:16:31.764 --> 00:16:36.200
And you are the criminal, Smith.

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:40.524
Ah, but you can't prove it!

00:16:40.584 --> 00:16:44.020
And now you need me!

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:50.373
Give me water! Holmes says weakly.
 
00:16:50.433 --> 00:16:52.094
All right,

00:16:52.154 --> 00:16:56.996
but only because I want to say something to you.

00:16:57.056 --> 00:17:04.759
Your illness is from men working near the river, your friend says.

00:17:04.819 --> 00:17:07.220
But that's wrong.

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:12.582
You aren't very quick. Are you, Holmes?
 
00:17:12.642 --> 00:17:15.415
I can't think.

00:17:15.474 --> 00:17:18.296
You must help me.

00:17:18.356 --> 00:17:20.898
Think carefully.

00:17:20.958 --> 00:17:27.331
Think about a box arriving here last Wednesday.

00:17:27.391 --> 00:17:34.592
A box ... yes, I remember now.
   
00:17:34.652 --> 00:17:40.320
The spring in the box on my hand ...

00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:42.582
the blood!

00:17:42.642 --> 00:17:45.234
That's right.

00:17:45.294 --> 00:17:52.317
And there are microbes of your illness on that spring.

00:17:52.377 --> 00:17:56.339
This box is the only proof,

00:17:56.399 --> 00:17:59.700
and I'm taking it with me!

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:04.300
Now you know the truth.

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:10.951
Now you can die!

00:18:10.971 --> 00:18:15.852
More light, says Holmes weakly.

00:18:15.912 --> 00:18:23.584
Smith moves, and suddenly, there is more light in the room.

00:18:23.644 --> 00:18:29.346
What more can I do for you? Smith asks.
 
00:18:29.406 --> 00:18:32.837
And more water, please,

00:18:32.898 --> 00:18:37.387
Holmes says. But what is happening?

00:18:37.407 --> 00:18:42.272
Holmes is speaking normally.

00:18:42.332 --> 00:18:46.195
His voice is not weak.

00:18:46.255 --> 00:18:51.780
Watson hears this, and he nearly cries out.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:19:06.200
He can feel Culverton Smith's shock.

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:21.500
Chapter Six. The truth. 

00:19:21.600 --> 00:19:23.744
What is this?

00:19:23.804 --> 00:19:25.936
Aren't you ill?

00:19:25.996 --> 00:19:30.070
Culverton Smith asks angrily.

00:19:30.130 --> 00:19:37.459
After three days without food or drink, I'm not very well.

00:19:37.519 --> 00:19:41.804
But I'm much better than you think.

00:19:41.864 --> 00:19:46.438
Holmes says in his normal voice.

00:19:46.498 --> 00:19:50.892
Ah, a friend is coming, I think.

00:19:50.952 --> 00:19:55.214
The light is telling him to come.

00:19:55.274 --> 00:20:01.940
The door opens, and Inspector Morton comes in.

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:06.034
This is your man, Inspector.

00:20:06.094 --> 00:20:08.000
Holmes says.

00:20:08.218 --> 00:20:13.180
I arrest you for the murder of Victor Savage,

00:20:13.240 --> 00:20:16.312
Morton says to Smith.

00:20:16.372 --> 00:20:20.803
He wants my murder too!

00:20:20.863 --> 00:20:23.054
Holmes laughs.

00:20:23.114 --> 00:20:27.256
The proof is in the box in his coat.

00:20:27.316 --> 00:20:32.142
But don't put your hand on it, Inspector.

00:20:32.202 --> 00:20:34.376
Smith cries.

00:20:34.436 --> 00:20:39.228
You can't prove anything, Holmes!

00:20:39.288 --> 00:20:44.500
Don't forget my friend, Dr Watson,

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:51.272
Holmes says. He can tell an interesting story.

00:20:51.332 --> 00:20:55.004
Come out, Watson!

00:20:55.064 --> 00:20:59.941
Morton leaves with Culverton Smith.

00:21:00.001 --> 00:21:05.890
Holmes dresses and then he talks to Watson.

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:09.542
I'm a good actor, Watson.

00:21:09.602 --> 00:21:17.356
And no food or drink for three days is easy for me.

00:21:17.416 --> 00:21:22.788
This yellow face is only make-up.

00:21:22.848 --> 00:21:28.598
You can't come near me and not see the truth.

00:21:28.658 --> 00:21:33.637
So my illness is contagious.

00:21:33.697 --> 00:21:39.430
Bad light in the room helps with my act.

00:21:39.490 --> 00:21:46.192
Victor Savage's murder is all about money.

00:21:46.252 --> 00:21:53.576
Money is more important than family to Culverton Smith.

00:21:53.636 --> 00:21:58.426
I get some strange things at this house.

00:21:58.486 --> 00:22:05.546
Happily, I always open them very carefully.

00:22:05.606 --> 00:22:10.538
Now we must go to Scotland Yard.

00:22:10.598 --> 00:22:34.000
After that, I want to sit down with you and eat until midnight.